<!--
     SPDX-FileCopyrightText: The LineageOS Project
     SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

     malbec (Lenovo TB390FU) — hardware-backed keystore version.

     There is no file for this in frameworks/native/data/etc/: the version is a
     property of the KeyMint TA in the TrustZone image, so only the device can
     state it. 300 means KeyMint 3.0, and it is not a guess — the vendor manifest
     declares `android.hardware.security.keymint` at AIDL version 3 for both
     IKeyMintDevice/default and IRemotelyProvisionedComponent/default (checked
     against the running device, session 25), and the framework maps AIDL
     version N to feature version N00.

     Content is byte-identical to what Lenovo's vendor image declares at this
     path; it lives here rather than in proprietary-files.txt because a feature
     file that arrives via the blob list can be dropped by a re-extraction with
     no build error. work/OPEN-ISSUES.md #64.

     ⚠️ If a future ZUI drop moves the TA to KeyMint 4, this number has to move
     with it — the pairing to assert is `vintf dm | grep -A2 security.keymint`
     against the value below. Declaring a version the TA does not implement makes
     apps that gate on hardware_keystore>=N take a path the device cannot serve.
-->
<permissions>
    <feature name="android.hardware.hardware_keystore" version="300" />
</permissions>
